/* book exam traps: Treating Γ as a real number: Γ is complex. Its magnitude sets VSWR and reflected power, but its phase sets where the voltage maxima and minima sit. | Writing VSWR = (1 − |Γ|)/(1 + |Γ|): the correct form is VSWR = (1 + |Γ|)/(1 − |Γ|), so VSWR is at least 1 and becomes infinite at total reflection. | Calling return loss negative: return loss = −20 log10|Γ| dB is already positive for a passive load; 6.99 dB is correct, −6.99 dB is not. | Confusing return loss with mismatch loss: return loss uses |Γ| and 20 log, while mismatch loss uses 1 − |Γ|² and 10 log. | Thinking VSWR changes along a lossless line: only the phase of Γ rotates; |Γ| and VSWR stay the same. */
